# Release & JetBrains Marketplace conventions

Apply whenever editing `waaagh/src/main/resources/META-INF/plugin.xml`, cutting a release, or
touching the release pipeline. (Build/run conventions live in `AGENTS.md`.)

## Branding / naming
- The brand is **WAAAGH!!!** — use it (with the `!!!`) in `README*.md` and in the plugin `<description>` prose.
- The plugin.xml `<name>` MUST be **`WAAAGH`** (no `!`). JetBrains Marketplace names only allow letters,
  digits, spaces and `` .,+_-/:()#'&[]| `` — `!` is rejected on upload.
- Do NOT change the plugin `<id>` (`com.waaagh`) — it identifies the Marketplace plugin (id `33496`).

## `<description>` (Marketplace "Overview")
- The check runs on the **rendered** description text (HTML tags stripped, entities decoded):
  its first 40 characters must match `^[\w\s\p{Punct}\u2013\u2014]{40,}` — i.e. ASCII
  letters/digits/whitespace/punctuation (or `–` `—`). Non-ASCII symbols such as `↔` (even written
  as `&harr;`), CJK characters or typographic quotes break the check if they appear within those
  first 40 rendered characters — keep them out of the opening line / first sentence.
- Keep it **bilingual** with a clear split; mark the Chinese block with `<b>中文</b>`, separated by
  `<br><br>`. Do NOT use `<hr>` as the divider — the Marketplace renderer strips it.
- `docs/marketplace-description.html` is the paste-ready copy for the Marketplace web editor
  (the page description is maintained separately from the uploaded zip). Update it together with
  `plugin.xml` whenever the description changes.
- Positioning: an IntelliJ IDEA **plugin collection**; popular tools may later be spun out as
  standalone plugins. Keep the description focused on features and usage — do not add statements
  about how the code is written or maintained.

## `<change-notes>` (Marketplace "What's New")
- List **only user-facing feature/behavior changes**.
- Do NOT add entries for release-pipeline / CI / signing changes, Marketplace-metadata or listing fixes,
  or other non-functional plumbing.
- A version that only changes docs / listing / pipeline gets **no** What's New entry.

## Versioning & publishing
- Release by pushing a git tag **`v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`**. CI (`.github/workflows/build-plugin.yml`)
  builds the plugin, creates a GitHub Release, and publishes to Marketplace. The version is derived from the
  tag via `-PpluginVersion`, so do NOT hand-edit `<version>` in plugin.xml for releases.
- **Never reuse a published version/tag** — Marketplace rejects duplicate versions; always bump to the next unused patch.
- Plugin **signing is optional**. Keep the guarded `signPlugin` block in `waaagh/build.gradle.kts` (only sign
  when `CERTIFICATE_CHAIN` and `PRIVATE_KEY` are non-blank). Publishing unsigned is fine; do not make signing mandatory.
- Marketplace "Overview" / "What's New" only refresh after a new version is uploaded, and may lag while JetBrains processes it.

## Secrets (repo → Settings → Secrets)
- `PUBLISH_TOKEN` — required for Marketplace auto-publish (absent ⇒ the publish step skips).
- `CERTIFICATE_CHAIN` / `PRIVATE_KEY` / `PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD` — optional; presence auto-enables signing.
